    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="structllvm_1_1bitfields__details_1_1_compressor" kindref="compound">Compressor</ref></computeroutput> is used to manipulate the bits of a (possibly signed) integer type so it can be packed and unpacked into a <computeroutput>bits</computeroutput> sized integer, <computeroutput><ref refid="structllvm_1_1bitfields__details_1_1_compressor" kindref="compound">Compressor</ref></computeroutput> is specialized on signed-ness so no runtime cost is incurred. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>pack</computeroutput> method also checks that the passed in <computeroutput>UserValue</computeroutput> is valid. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
